      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Goldens Bridge sits beside the Croton River and lies adjacent to Interstate 684, placing it in western Westchester County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldens_Bridge%2C_New_York",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The hamlet’s name has evolved over time, appearing as Coldens Bridge, Goldings Bridge, and Goldens Bridge on early maps.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldens_Bridge%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original bridge was washed away by floods and rebuilt multiple times until the Croton Watershed dams controlled the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldens_Bridge%2C_New_York",
